@kirkchinese/dsh-recollect README · 已知限制：- DSH 在上下文溢出时，会在同一步内压缩并重试，不再经过注入流程，所以这一次重试看不到指令块，要到下一步才补回。
- headless 模式在一轮结束后立即退出，后台提取不会运行。
- 整理锁的做法是写入 PID 后回读校验，不是原子操作；两个宿主进程同时整理同一目录时可能冲突。同一个 DSH 主目录请不要同时运行两个宿主进程。

@kirkchinese/dsh-recollect README · Why：- **records** who the user is, feedback on how they want work done, project context and pointers to external resources, at the right moments;
- sees the memory index in each new session and reads or recalls memory bodies when relevant;
- verifies a memory before recommending from it, because memories go stale.

@kirkchinese/dsh-recollect README · or a release tag from the repository：dsh plugin --profile web add "git+https://github.com/kirkchinese/DSH-Recollect.git#v0.5.0"
```

Restart DSH and reload the page. New sessions use Recollect. It takes over instruction-file loading and filters out what DSH's built-in AGENTS.md loader injects, so no file is loaded twice.

@kirkchinese/dsh-recollect README · Installing on Windows：- Background extraction and dream helpers only allow bash read-only commands (plus restricted memory deletion). DSH uses pwsh on Windows, so these helpers cannot run shell commands there. Both features are off by default; ordinary memory reads/writes, sharing and imports are unaffected.
- `instructions.managedDirs` defaults to `/etc/claude-code`, which normally does not exist on Windows. Set a real absolute directory if organization policies are needed.
- Slugs follow Claude Code's rule: `C:\Users\me\proj` becomes `C--Users-me-proj`, so per-project sharing resolves to the same memories.
